at period.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Kills the administered-wage-jump mechanism that is the entire reason my CQ1 is 20 rather than 11. CQ1 conjunct B falls from 0.28 to ~0.12 and CQ1 drops from 20 to ~10, i.e. to the Wave-1 centre. Hypothesis plank (a) falls from 7 to ~4. Mildly lowers my OECD core path (care is 0.15 of core at 3.6% in my build), taking CQ2 to ~31 and CQ6-C to ~23.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Strict operational OECD-38 + China data-centre electricity consumption, on the IEA's own reporting basis, is at or below 650 TWh for calendar 2032 (against ~365 TWh in 2024), OR announced hyperscaler capacity is written down by 20%+ AND measured operational TWh falls year-on-year in any year 2029-2033.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my contrarian coupling call that AI-Q3 is TOO LOW (I say P50 ~1,050-1,100 TWh against the unanimous Wave-1 shade-down to 820-900) and specifically my claim that an impairment event impairs the accounting, not the kilowatt-hours. The electricity-pass-through leg of my hot-core path weakens, CQ2 falls to ~30 and CQ6-C to ~21; CQ3 P50 falls ~0.1 through the capital-deepening term; CQ6-D rises to ~14. The unanimous Wave-1 read would be the right one and my central coupling finding would be the ensemble's worst input.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 2 premortem seat, effort 'inflation'."}}